		"roundedEdges":true,
		"lore":[
			"Fort Vogelsangbay is one of the oldest surviving",
			"buildings in the town and was constructed in 1890",
			"by the German colonial Schutztruppe under Captain",
			"Curt von François as a fort to secure German presence",
			"in the region. Originally serving as a military",
			"headquarters and barracks during the early colonial",
			"occupation of what was then German South West Africa,",
			"it played a central role in the establishment of",
			"colonial administration in Vogelsangbay.",
			"Over time, as its military importance declined,",
			"the building was repurposed several times,",
			"including as a school and administrative facility.",
			"Today, after restoration efforts, it functions as part",
			"of Namibia’s National Museum complex, preserving and",
			"exhibiting historical artifacts that reflect both the",
			"colonial period and broader Namibian history.",
